### Mock payment gateway (Lab 2) – called by the REST Connector of task "Process payment".
### Mock tokens only: never send real card numbers or credentials.

### 1. Approved charge
POST http://localhost:8082/mock/payment-gateway/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-API-1", "amount": 215.76, "currency": "EUR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_approve", "customerReference": "CUST-0001"}

### 2. Declined charge (HTTP 200, status DECLINED)
POST http://localhost:8082/mock/payment-gateway/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-API-2", "amount": 553.79, "currency": "EUR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_decline_funds", "customerReference": "CUST-0004"}

### 3. Gateway outage (HTTP 503) – same effect as the fault switch below
POST http://localhost:8082/mock/payment-gateway/charges
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "ORD-API-3", "amount": 409.79, "currency": "EUR", "paymentToken": "tok_test_gateway_error", "customerReference": "CUST-0001"}

### 4. Break / repair the gateway (fault injection)
POST http://localhost:8082/admin/faults/payment-gateway-down?enabled=true

###
POST http://localhost:8082/admin/faults/payment-gateway-down?enabled=false

### 5. Break / repair the inventory service
POST http://localhost:8082/admin/faults/inventory-service-down?enabled=true

###
POST http://localhost:8082/admin/faults/inventory-service-down?enabled=false

### 6. Current fault switches
GET http://localhost:8082/admin/faults

### 7. Start an order instance via the Camunda REST API
POST http://localhost:8080/v2/process-instances
Content-Type: application/json

{"processDefinitionId": "order-fulfilment", "variables": {"orderId": "ORD-HTTP-1", "customerReference": "CUST-0001", "productId": "PRD-1001", "quantity": 2, "deliveryPreference": "STANDARD", "paymentToken": "tok_test_approve"}}
